The binaries in native/lib/ are built from three third-party hash
implementations, kept as git submodules in native/vendor/ at the commits
below: the versions SpeeduPy's measurements used. Their licenses apply to
their code and travel with the binaries in this file, since a clone without
the submodules has the binaries but not the sources. The wrappers in
native/src/ and native/museair/ are part of SpeeduPy and under its license
(LICENSE at the root of the repository).

The submodules are never moved to another commit silently: a new commit
changes the hash values, and MuseAir's later versions are a different
algorithm. native/README.md says how to rebuild the binaries.


